## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses a candidate's ability to negotiate and mediate cross-disciplinary conflicts, surface underlying interests, and implement a plan with feedback loops in high-stakes scenarios involving safety constraints.

## Key Concepts

- Interest-based negotiation
- Mediation with established ground rules
- Stakeholder mapping and surfacing underlying concerns
- Actionable planning with clear accountability

## Code Example

```javascript
function surfaceInterests(parties) {
  const interests = {};
  parties.forEach(party => {
    interests[party.name] = party.statedPosition;
    interests[party.name] = party.underlyingInterest;
  });
  return interests;
}

function mediateSession(parties, constraints) {
  const commonInterests = findCommonGround(parties);
  return createPhasedPlan(commonInterests, constraints);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle a situation where neither party is willing to compromise?
- What would you do if safety constraints required a significant scope change mid-project?
- How do you ensure accountability when team priorities shift?

